WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:02.640
Have you ever wondered

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:06.560
if there are more natural ways
to lower your high blood pressure,

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.520
guard against Alzheimer's,
lose weight, and feel better?

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.720
Well, it turns out there is!

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.200
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.240
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:20.880
Today, we continue our series

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:25.280
on ways to boost the production of
the important metabolic enzyme NAD+

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:30.160
by reviewing a supplement called NMN.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.880
Both NR and NMN have been shown
to have beneficial effects in rodents,

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.360
though they haven’t
been tested side-by-side.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:40.240
Both precursors raise blood
levels of NAD+ in people

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:44.080
but similarly haven’t been pitted
head-to-head against one another.

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:46.960
One potential advantage
of NMN over NR

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:49.360
is that it may be more
stable in the bloodstream.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:54.480
In mouse blood at least, within an hour,
most NR is converted into NAM,

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:57.760
whereas NMN levels remain steady.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:02.320
You could also argue that NMN is better
because it’s a direct precursor of NAD+,

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:05.840
whereas NR first has
to be converted to NMN;

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:08.880
so, we might as well just
take NMN in the first place.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:12.560
Ironically, the exact opposite
argument can also be made

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:17.440
based on the inability of NMN to
pass through cell membranes.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:22.080
Structurally, NMN is just NR with
a phosphate group attached to it.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:25.920
The phosphate charge prevents NMN
from passing in and out of cells;

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:30.880
so, to get inside a cell, NMN first
has to be converted into NR.

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:35.440
Then, once inside, the NR can turn
back into NMN and make NAD+.

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:41.120
So, if NMN first has to be converted
into NR for cell entry, the argument goes,

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:44.080
maybe you might as well
just take NR to begin with,

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:47.040
because there’s no
NMN transporter.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.320
Or is there?

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:52.560
An NMN transporter was recently
described (at least in mouse intestine);

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:55.600
so, maybe NMN is
able to skip the NR step

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:58.880
and pass directly into cells
to make NAD+ after all.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:04.400
However, the evidence that such a NMN
transporter exists remains controversial.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.960
NMN boasts a long list of
rodent healthspan benefits,

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:14.080
but, unlike NR, has yet to demonstrate
an extension of mammalian lifespan.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:15.840
What about in people?

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:20.160
There have just been a few human
NMN studies published to date.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:22.160
One small study of healthy
middle-aged men

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:25.600
found that various single doses
had no apparent effect

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:28.640
on any of the measured variables,
including retinal eye function,

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:30.560
sleep quality, heart rate,
blood pressure,

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:32.640
oxygenation,
or body temperature.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:36.720
A 12-week study of daily NMN supplementation
in middle-aged men and women

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:40.560
similarly found no significant
effects on any outcome,

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.720
including lean mass,
muscle mass, body fat,

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.840
blood sugars, cholesterol,
or insulin sensitivity.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:50.080
NMN did boost blood NAD+ levels,
though they peaked after the first month

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:52.560
and then trended down
for months two and three;

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:56.000
so, there may have been an
adaptive drop in NAD+ synthesis

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.320
as was suspected with NR.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:03.920
Like NR, NMN also fails to
raise NAD+ in muscle tissue.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:05.920
One study evocatively entitled,

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:11.440
“Nicotinamide Mononucleotide Supplementation
Enhances Aerobic Capacity in Amateur Runners,”

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:14.880
tested three different doses of
NMN versus placebo for six weeks

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:17.840
among young and middle-
aged recreational runners.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:24.320
Aerobic capacity was increased at one
ventilatory threshold, but not the other.

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:27.280
No overall benefit for aerobic
capacity or peak power

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:31.200
or any of another ten measures of
cardiopulmonary function was found.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:32.640
If you measure enough things,

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:35.520
statistical outliers,
both positive and negative ones,

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:37.200
can just pop up as flukes.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.760
For example, the researchers
noted significant improvement

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:42.560
in the single-leg stance test,

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:47.120
but the NMN had no significant effect on
any of the other physical function tests.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.640
And upon closer inspection,

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:53.120
the apparent single-leg balance benefit
was only found in the middle-dose group

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:55.360
compared to the high-dose group,

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:59.920
because the high-dose group ended up
doing slightly worse compared to baseline.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:04.400
No significant effect was found for
any of the doses compared to placebo.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:09.680
A similar issue can be found in a 12-week
study of NMN supplementation in older adults.

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:12.880
The NMN company-funded
authors concluded

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:18.240
that NMN “improved lower limb function
and reduced drowsiness in older adults.”

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:21.760
But it failed to significantly
affect 16 additional measures,

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:25.760
including other tests of lower
limb function and fatigue.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:31.520
There are so few NMN studies that this
kind of shotgun approach is understandable,

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:35.040
casting the widest possible net
for effects to be further tested,

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:40.320
but on their own cannot be presented
as convincing proof of efficacy.

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:44.000
All of the above NMN studies
were on healthy individuals.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:48.640
What about testing NMN on those who
are already metabolically compromised?

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:51.600
Overweight or obese postmenopausal
women with prediabetes

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:55.200
were randomized to NMN
or placebo for 10 weeks.

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:58.720
NMN didn’t seem to affect
body weight or composition,

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:01.680
liver fat, blood pressure,
or a dozen other metabolic variables,

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:04.960
but it did improve
muscle insulin sensitivity,

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:10.720
though not enough to affect insulin levels
or short- or long-term blood sugar control.

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:16.480
This may be because insulin sensitivity
in the liver and body fat remained unchanged.

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:19.840
NMN also appeared to have no
effect on mitochondrial function

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:23.680
or muscle strength,
fatigability, or recovery.

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:29.200
In terms of safety, NMN shills speak of it as
being naturally found in fruits and vegetables,

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:33.280
but even the most concentrated sources
(edamame, avocado, and broccoli)

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:39.520
have over a hundred times less per serving
than the typical NMN supplement dose.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:44.400
The same could be said for NR in milk
(human and otherwise).

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:49.760
There are safety evaluations for NMN
on rats and dogs, but unlike NR,

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:56.560
supplemental doses of NMN have yet to
be shown as safe for human consumption.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:59.040
There are rodent studies
showing that NMN

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:02.400
may have negative metabolic
consequences compared to placebo,

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:07.200
but the most serious concern
is nerve degeneration.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:11.200
The accumulation of NMN
in nerve cells is toxic.

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:13.920
Since NR is converted into NMN,

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:17.920
this is a major concern for
NR supplementation as well.

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:20.960
The type of nerve damage,
axon degeneration,

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:25.600
is a major contributor to a variety
of neurodegenerative disorders.

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:31.600
Blocking an NMN-synthesizing enzyme
appeared to help damaged neurons in vitro,

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:34.960
protection that’s abolished
by adding NMN back,

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:39.600
and adding an enzyme that chews up
NMN was also found to be protective,

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:44.960
further supporting a theory of degenerative
effects of accumulating NMN.

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:48.160
However, clinical effects
remain theoretical,

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:53.680
as these adverse effects have only been
demonstrated in fish, mice, and petri dishes.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:58.320
Of course, NMN supplements may not
even have NMN in the first place.

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:03.120
ChromaDex, which sells the rival
supplement Tru Niagen (a form of NR),

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:08.160
claims to have tested the 22 NMN brands
with the highest market share on Amazon

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:12.080
and found that most had
virtually no NMN at all.

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:16.320
Ironically, many of the apparently fake
NMN products displayed quote-unquote

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:21.200
“certificates of analysis” and carried
hundreds or thousands of positive reviews.

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:28.480
Evidently, only 3 out of 22 were found to contain
as much NMN as advertised on their label.

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:31.600
Of course, ChromaDex isn’t
above being shady itself;

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:34.800
it’s been accused of making
hyped false claims for Tru Niagen

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:38.560
by both the FDA and the
Better Business Bureau.

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:43.600
In short, NR has been demonstrated
to be relatively safe but not effective,

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:49.600
and neither safety nor efficacy
has been established for NMN.

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:52.880
What about all the other purported
NAD-boosting supplements?

00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:54.960
Let’s find out.

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:58.400
Taking niacin,
also called nicotinic acid,

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:00.560
would be about 50 times
more efficient

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:03.040
than taking
the amino acid tryptophan

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:04.240
to boost NAD+,

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:06.080
because only about two percent
of tryptophan

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:08.480
is converted into niacin.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:10.240
Also, tryptophan didn't work

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:12.640
to improve mitochondrial
or muscle function

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:15.120
in physically compromised
older adults,

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:18.240
even when combined
with niacin or nicotinamide.

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:20.080
And side effects
of taking tryptophan

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:22.320
include belching and gas,
blurred vision,

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:25.040
diarrhea, dizziness,
drowsiness, dry mouth,

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:25.920
headache, heartburn,

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:28.320
and potentially
a life-threatening condition

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:32.320
known as eosinophilia-myalgia
syndrome, or EMS.

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:36.080
There was an epidemic of EMS
tied to tryptophan supplements

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:38.720
from a single supplier
back in 1989

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:40.000
that led to their removal

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:43.360
from the market
for about 15 years.

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:45.760
Some sort of contaminant
was suspected,

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:47.760
but the cause
remains a mystery.

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:49.520
To this day,
tryptophan supplements

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:52.240
continue to be tainted
with impurities,

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:54.400
with at least one case
of EMS reported

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:56.960
decades after
the initial epidemic.

00:08:56.960 --> 00:09:00.240
A case of EMS tied to
a bizarre weight loss diet

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:03.120
involving hundreds of cups
(~48 L) of cashews,

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:04.960
a rich source of tryptophan,

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:06.480
suggests the syndrome
can be caused

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:09.360
by excess tryptophan directly.

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:10.480
If anything,

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:14.080
tryptophan restriction
may be beneficial.

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:15.040
Nearly 50 years ago,

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:16.960
it was demonstrated
that restricting

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:19.520
dietary tryptophan
reduced cancer rates

00:09:19.520 --> 00:09:21.600
and increased
the lifespans of rats

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:23.760
and, subsequently, mice.

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:25.760
Vegetarians and vegans
both appear to have

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:28.160
significantly lower intakes
of tryptophan,

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:30.720
but only in vegans
does this translate

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:32.800
to lower
tryptophan blood levels,

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:34.160
though presumably not

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:37.760
if they were to take
tryptophan supplements.

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:40.560
What about taking NAD+ directly?

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:42.000
This isn't practical

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:44.880
because of instability
and poor bioavailability.

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:48.720
NAD+ is vulnerable to heat,
pH, light, and oxygen,

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:51.040
requiring dark desiccant storage

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:54.560
at ideally 20 degrees (-29°C)
below freezing.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:56.960
NAD+ can be given intravenously,

00:09:56.960 --> 00:09:58.800
a practice started
in the 1950s

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:01.760
as an "underground" treatment
for alcoholism,

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:03.360
but when taken orally,

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:06.000
NAD may be broken down
in the alkaline environment

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:08.640
of the small intestine,
and NADH,

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:10.800
the so-called "reduced" form
of NAD+,

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:12.960
is broken down
in the acidic conditions

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:14.240
of the stomach.

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:17.680
(In organic chemistry,
the gain of a hydrogen atom

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:19.920
is said to quote-unquote
"reduce" the molecule,

00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:24.400
so NADH
is the reduced form of NAD+).

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:27.200
Enteric forms of NAD+
could potentially survive

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:30.480
the digestive tract, but,
with the exception of neurons,

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:33.920
NAD can't cross
into mammalian cells.

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:36.480
This is why
NAD+ precursor supplements,

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:39.840
like NMN and NR,
were developed.

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:42.400
Also, there are evidently
(unpublished) data

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:43.680
showing that straight NAD+

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:46.960
can cause severe hyperglycemia
in mice.

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:48.800
Has it been tested in people?

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:50.560
NAD+ boosting supplements

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:52.240
have been found
to improve the learning

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:55.120
and memory of rodent models
of Alzheimer's disease

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:56.480
in the lab.

00:10:56.480 --> 00:11:00.880
In 1995, case reports
of apparent benefit of NADH

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:03.040
for Alzheimer's disease
were published.

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:06.560
By the next year, an open-label
pilot study was published,

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:08.720
suggesting it had
a protective effect,

00:11:08.720 --> 00:11:10.720
but without
a placebo control group,

00:11:10.720 --> 00:11:12.400
the only conclusion
that could be drawn

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:14.240
was to study it further,

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:15.920
especially since
a similar study

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:17.040
with the same dose

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:18.800
over approximately
the same period

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:22.480
found no evidence
of any cognitive effects.

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:25.360
There have been
two randomized, double-blind,

00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:26.640
placebo-controlled trials

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:29.200
of NAD precursors
for Alzheimer's.

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:32.160
One found no benefit
for memory, attention,

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:34.720
or clinician ratings
of dementia severity,

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:36.720
but did maybe find
less of a drop

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:38.480
in one dementia rating scale

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:41.840
after six months
of 10 milligrams a day of NADH.

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:44.480
The other, a six-month study
of nicotinamide,

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:47.600
failed to find
any clinical effects.

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:50.800
What about trying
NMNH and NRH,

00:11:50.800 --> 00:11:54.000
the reduced forms
of NMN and NR?

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:56.640
They both appear
to boost NAD+ higher

00:11:56.640 --> 00:11:58.720
than their
non-reduced counterparts.

00:11:58.720 --> 00:12:02.080
In vitro,
NMNH can raise NAD+ levels

00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:04.640
up to 10 times higher than NMN,

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:08.800
and NRH (also known as
dihydronicotinamide riboside)

00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:12.640
is up to about 50 times
more potent than NR.

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:15.520
There are concerns
about stability of NRH

00:12:15.520 --> 00:12:16.560
outside the body,

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:18.880
since it's sensitive to oxygen
and moisture,

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:20.160
but within the body,

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:21.920
NRH may be more stable,

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:24.240
not rapidly devolving
into nicotinamide,

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:26.880
like NR does
(at least in mouse blood).

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:28.640
However, unlike NR,

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:30.560
NRH does not appear
to be able

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:34.480
to significantly increase levels
in mouse muscles.

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:37.440
NRH is said to have
a "spectacular potency"

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:39.120
for increasing NAD+ levels,

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:42.480
perhaps the most potent
precursor discovered to date.

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:45.120
This may not necessarily be
a good thing.

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:47.760
The extreme boost
afforded by NRH

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:51.520
had detrimental consequences
in human liver cells in vitro,

00:12:51.520 --> 00:12:53.760
resulting from
an excessive accumulation

00:12:53.760 --> 00:12:55.040
of free radicals.

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:56.160
In addition to oxidation,

00:12:56.160 --> 00:12:59.360
NRH was also found
promote inflammation.

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:01.600
Pro-inflammatory effects
were noted for NRH

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:06.800
on human immune cells in vitro
(but not for NMN, NAM, or NR).

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:10.240
Because it appears that NMNH
is converted to NRH

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:11.520
to enter cells,

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:13.600
these potentially
deleterious effects

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:15.920
may be shared
by NMNH as well

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:19.520
(though this has yet
to be tested).

